Let $(M_n)$ be a martingale and $T$ a stopping time. Then $E[M_T] = E[M_0]$ in each of the following cases:
1. $T \le N$ for some constant $N$;
2. $P(T < \infty) = 1$ and $|M_{n \wedge T}| \le K$ for all $n$, for some constant $K$;
3. $E[T] < \infty$ and $|M_{n} - M_{n-1}| \le K$ for all $n$, for some constant $K$.

